                branch_unit_id="DOC-054-BU-01",
                raw_text=doc054_text,
                snippet="System Design and Technical Logic\n\nVisual Diagram: A simple diagram showing how inputs, microcontrollers, and outputs connect, \nas to quickly understand the project's logic and hardware layout.\u00a0\n\nHow It Works: Step by step explanation of what happens when the device operates, written in \nclear logical steps.\n\nMain Components List: Summary of primary hardware parts, modules, materials, and software \nplatforms used.\n\n\n\n\n\nImplementation Plan and Budget\nProof of Concept Scope: Clear explanation of what exact features will be \n\nphysically built and shown at the exhibition booth versus conceptual \nfeatures.\n\nBill of Materials and Budget: Simple table listing parts, quantity, source, unit \nprice, and with a budget range of Rp.150,000 - Rp.300,000.\n\nDesign Iterations and SWOT Analysis: A breakdown of initial design concepts \nevaluating their strengths, weaknesses, opportunities, and threats, including \na clear justification for why the final iteration was selected for construction.\u00a0\n\n\n\n\n\n@techtonic.ui techtonicieeesbui2025@gmail.com\n 24\n\n\n\nechtonic 3.0\n#TechForTomorrow\n\nImpact and Practical Use\n\nBenefits: Practical advantages of the solution for users, community, or the environment.\n\nFuture Ideas: Simple ideas for how the project could be improved or expanded if given more \ntime or budget in the future.",
