                raw_text=doc054_text,
                snippet="Writing Rules and Formatting Standards\n\nDocument Layout and Page Setup\n\nFont: Times New Roman across the entire document.\n\nHierarchy: Document Title in 24 point bold centered, Section Headings in 10 point \nsmall caps centered, Subheadings in 10 point italic left aligned, Body text in 10 \npoint regular fully justified.\n\nPage Setup: Standard A4 or Letter with 0.75 inch margins, single or 1.15 line \nspacing. \n\n\n\nStylistic and Tone Rules\n\nTone: Objective third person voice, avoiding personal pronouns like I or we where \npossible.\n\nTerminology: Standard SI units and fully written acronyms on first use, such as \nProof of Concept.\n\n\n@techtonic.ui techtonicieeesbui2025@gmail.com\n 26\n\n\n\nechtonic 3.0\n3\n\nPRELIMINARY ROUND\nWriting Rules and Formatting Standards\n\nVisuals, Equations, and Tables\n\nFigures: High resolution block diagrams and flowcharts with captions placed \nbelow the figure.\n\nTables: Captions placed above the table in small caps.\n\nFormulas and Equations: Centered on their own line with right aligned equation \nnumbers in parentheses, using proper scientific notation and standard SI units \nfor all mathematical and scientific values.\u00a0\n\n\n\nCitation and Reference Style\n\nIn Text Citations: Bracketed numbers sequential to the reference list.\n\nReference Format: Listed at the end following standard IEEE reference formatting \nfor web articles, datasheets, or publications.",
